{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1795805314","published":"2026-11-27T18:51:05Z","modified":"2026-11-28T00:58:16.576969185Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-101296","CVE-2026-101356","CVE-2026-76183","CVE-2026-77791","CVE-2026-78383","CVE-2026-79677","CVE-2026-86350"],"summary":"tomcat: Fix of 7 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-76183: do not parse WebSocket request paths as URI templates, so a\n  path segment such as {b} no longer matches a literal segment of an endpoint\n  path that a security constraint does not cover (upstream tomcat 9.0.122)\n- CVE-2026-77791: sleep instead of yielding while a WebSocket close message\n  waits for a pending write, so that the waiting thread no longer keeps a CPU\n  busy (upstream tomcat 9.0.122)\n- CVE-2026-78383: do not wait for the request body of an AJP request that ended\n  in error, and close the connection after such a request instead of reading\n  an unread body packet as a new request (upstream tomcat 9.0.122 and 32af9c0b\n  from the 9.0.x branch)\n- CVE-2026-79677: track every WebSocket endpoint that waits for a non-blocking\n  write, so that write timeouts are no longer lost (upstream tomcat 9.0.122)\n- CVE-2026-86350: validate HTTP/2 header fields after decoding them and keep\n  decoding the header block after an invalid field, so the HPACK state stays in\n  sync and later requests on the connection get their own header fields\n  (upstream tomcat 9.0.122)\n- CVE-2026-101296: always use a simple bind when JNDIRealm checks a password by\n  binding as the user (upstream tomcat 9.0.123)\n- CVE-2026-101356: treat an error raised after startAsync() as an asynchronous\n  error, and do not return the request and response of an HTTP/2 stream to the\n  pool while the application may still use them (after a timeout or an I/O\n  error, or while asynchronous processing of a request in an error state is\n  still running), so that they are not given to another request (upstream\n  tomcat 9.0.123, and 88409edb and 981efdbb from the 9.0.x branch)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"tomcat","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.8","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/tomcat?distro=almalinux-9.8"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:9.0.121-1.el9_8.tuxcare.els3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/tuxcare9.8esu/CLSA-2026-1795805314.json"}},{"package":{"name":"tomcat-admin-webapps","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.8","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/tomcat-admin-webapps?distro=almalinux-9.8"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:9.0.121-1.el9_8.tuxcare.els3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/tuxcare9.8esu/CLSA-2026-1795805314.json"}},{"package":{"name":"tomcat-docs-webapp","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.8","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/tomcat-docs-webapp?distro=almalinux-9.8"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:9.0.121-1.el9_8.tuxcare.els3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/tuxcare9.8esu/CLSA-2026-1795805314.json"}},{"package":{"name":"tomcat-el-3.0-api","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.8","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/tomcat-el-3.0-api?distro=almalinux-9.8"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:9.0.121-1.el9_8.tuxcare.els3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/tuxcare9.8esu/CLSA-2026-1795805314.json"}},{"package":{"name":"tomcat-jsp-2.3-api","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.8","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/tomcat-jsp-2.3-api?distro=almalinux-9.8"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:9.0.121-1.el9_8.tuxcare.els3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/tuxcare9.8esu/CLSA-2026-1795805314.json"}},{"package":{"name":"tomcat-lib","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.8","purl":"pkg